        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Israel, Lebanon extending ceasefire, US says, despite new Israeli strikes Middle East Issued on: 16/05/2026 - 08:25 Israel and Lebanon agreed to extend a ceasefire and hold expanded talks on a political settlement, the US announced days before the April 17 ceasefire was set to expire. The announcement came even as Israel carried out new strikes in southern Lebanon that it insists are not subject to the truce. Israel has been pounding Lebanon and invaded its south in response to fire from Hezbollah since early March. Abu Dhabi 'doesn't want to appear too much in cooperation with Israel,' analyst says 14/05/2026 Middle East Iran accuses United Arab Emirates of being 'active partner' in US-Israeli war 14/05/2026 Middle East Trump says Xi offered help to open Hormuz, vowed not to arm Iran 14/05/2026 Middle East The Fatah party elects new central committee for the first time in 10 years 14/05/2026 Middle East Lebanese split over diplomatic normalisation amid Washington talks 14/05/2026 Middle East Israel-Lebanon ceasefire nears end: Will fresh talks lead to new truce? 14/05/2026 Middle East Did Israel tip Eurovision 2025 results? NYT report delves into voting data 14/05/2026 Middle East Netanyahu's coalition seeks to dissolve parliament and trigger early election in Israel 14/05/2026 Middle East Israel launches fresh strikes on Lebanon despite ceasefire and ongoing talks 14/05/2026 Middle East"
